INSERT RELATION INTO looks_like { id: looks_like:[disease:`tomato_bacterial_speck`, disease:`tomato_bacterial_spot`], in: disease:`tomato_bacterial_speck`, out: disease:`tomato_bacterial_spot`, how_to_tell: 'Hard to tell apart by eye, especially early, so a lab test is recommended to confirm. On leaves, speck makes tiny black specks, usually 2 mm across or less; bacterial spot leaf spots can grow to 3 to 5 mm, and their centres dry out and tear into holes, so the leaf looks tattered. On fruit, speck makes pinpoint black specks (under about 1 to 3 mm) that are only slightly raised, sit on the surface and can be scraped off with a fingernail; bacterial spot makes bigger spots (up to about 4 to 6 mm) that are raised and scabby and can turn brown and greasy-looking.' } RETURN NONE;
INSERT RELATION INTO looks_like { id: looks_like:[disease:`tomato_bacterial_speck`, disease:`tomato_early_blight`], in: disease:`tomato_bacterial_speck`, out: disease:`tomato_early_blight`, how_to_tell: 'Bacterial speck makes black specks, usually no more than 2 mm across, with a yellow halo. Early blight spots grow larger, become angular and show dark rings like a target. Early blight does not make the small black fruit specks typical of speck.' } RETURN NONE;
INSERT RELATION INTO looks_like { id: looks_like:[disease:`tomato_bacterial_speck`, disease:`tomato_septoria_leaf_spot`], in: disease:`tomato_bacterial_speck`, out: disease:`tomato_septoria_leaf_spot`, how_to_tell: 'Bacterial speck makes small black spots on the fruit. Septoria does not infect fruit. Septoria leaf spots have light tan centres with tiny black dots.' } RETURN NONE;
INSERT RELATION INTO looks_like { id: looks_like:[disease:`tomato_bacterial_spot`, disease:`tomato_bacterial_speck`], in: disease:`tomato_bacterial_spot`, out: disease:`tomato_bacterial_speck`, how_to_tell: 'Hard to tell apart by eye, especially early, so a lab test is recommended to confirm. On leaves, speck makes tiny black specks, usually 2 mm across or less; bacterial spot leaf spots can grow to 3 to 5 mm, and their centres dry out and tear into holes, so the leaf looks tattered. On fruit, speck makes pinpoint black specks (under about 1 to 3 mm) that are only slightly raised, sit on the surface and can be scraped off with a fingernail; bacterial spot makes bigger spots (up to about 4 to 6 mm) that are raised and scabby and can turn brown and greasy-looking.' } RETURN NONE;
INSERT RELATION INTO looks_like { id: looks_like:[disease:`tomato_bacterial_spot`, disease:`tomato_early_blight`], in: disease:`tomato_bacterial_spot`, out: disease:`tomato_early_blight`, how_to_tell: 'Young early blight spots can look like bacterial spot. Look for the dark target-like rings of early blight. Early blight does not make the small black fruit spots typical of bacterial spot.' } RETURN NONE;
INSERT RELATION INTO looks_like { id: looks_like:[disease:`tomato_bacterial_spot`, disease:`tomato_septoria_leaf_spot`], in: disease:`tomato_bacterial_spot`, out: disease:`tomato_septoria_leaf_spot`, how_to_tell: 'Bacterial spot makes small black spots on the fruit. Septoria does not infect fruit. Septoria leaf spots have light tan centres with tiny black dots.' } RETURN NONE;
INSERT RELATION INTO looks_like { id: looks_like:[disease:`tomato_early_blight`, disease:`tomato_bacterial_speck`], in: disease:`tomato_early_blight`, out: disease:`tomato_bacterial_speck`, how_to_tell: 'Bacterial speck makes black specks, usually no more than 2 mm across, with a yellow halo. Early blight spots grow larger, become angular and show dark rings like a target. Early blight does not make the small black fruit specks typical of speck.' } RETURN NONE;
INSERT RELATION INTO looks_like { id: looks_like:[disease:`tomato_early_blight`, disease:`tomato_bacterial_spot`], in: disease:`tomato_early_blight`, out: disease:`tomato_bacterial_spot`, how_to_tell: 'Young early blight spots can look like bacterial spot. Look for the dark target-like rings of early blight. Early blight does not make the small black fruit spots typical of bacterial spot.' } RETURN NONE;
INSERT RELATION INTO looks_like { id: looks_like:[disease:`tomato_early_blight`, disease:`tomato_late_blight`], in: disease:`tomato_early_blight`, out: disease:`tomato_late_blight`, how_to_tell: 'Early blight spots start on the older, lower leaves and grow dark rings inside them, like a target. Late blight starts as small, dark spots that look soaked with water. They quickly grow into large patches, with white mould at their edges on the underside of the leaf.' } RETURN NONE;
INSERT RELATION INTO looks_like { id: looks_like:[disease:`tomato_early_blight`, disease:`tomato_septoria_leaf_spot`], in: disease:`tomato_early_blight`, out: disease:`tomato_septoria_leaf_spot`, how_to_tell: 'Septoria spots have light tan centres with tiny black dots, best seen with a hand lens. Septoria rarely causes yellowing until spots are many. Early blight spots have dark rings like a target, and they grow larger and angular over time.' } RETURN NONE;
INSERT RELATION INTO looks_like { id: looks_like:[disease:`tomato_late_blight`, disease:`tomato_early_blight`], in: disease:`tomato_late_blight`, out: disease:`tomato_early_blight`, how_to_tell: 'Early blight spots start on the older, lower leaves and grow dark rings inside them, like a target. Late blight starts as small, dark spots that look soaked with water. They quickly grow into large patches, with white mould at their edges on the underside of the leaf.' } RETURN NONE;
INSERT RELATION INTO looks_like { id: looks_like:[disease:`tomato_late_blight`, disease:`tomato_leaf_mold`], in: disease:`tomato_late_blight`, out: disease:`tomato_leaf_mold`, how_to_tell: 'Both can show mould on the underside of the leaf. In leaf mold it is a gray, velvety growth covering the spots, and the top of the leaf has pale green to bright yellow spots. In late blight it is white mould at the edges of dark patches that look soaked with water.' } RETURN NONE;
INSERT RELATION INTO looks_like { id: looks_like:[disease:`tomato_leaf_mold`, disease:`tomato_late_blight`], in: disease:`tomato_leaf_mold`, out: disease:`tomato_late_blight`, how_to_tell: 'Both can show mould on the underside of the leaf. In leaf mold it is a gray, velvety growth covering the spots, and the top of the leaf has pale green to bright yellow spots. In late blight it is white mould at the edges of dark patches that look soaked with water.' } RETURN NONE;
INSERT RELATION INTO looks_like { id: looks_like:[disease:`tomato_septoria_leaf_spot`, disease:`tomato_bacterial_speck`], in: disease:`tomato_septoria_leaf_spot`, out: disease:`tomato_bacterial_speck`, how_to_tell: 'Bacterial speck makes small black spots on the fruit. Septoria does not infect fruit. Septoria leaf spots have light tan centres with tiny black dots.' } RETURN NONE;
INSERT RELATION INTO looks_like { id: looks_like:[disease:`tomato_septoria_leaf_spot`, disease:`tomato_bacterial_spot`], in: disease:`tomato_septoria_leaf_spot`, out: disease:`tomato_bacterial_spot`, how_to_tell: 'Bacterial spot makes small black spots on the fruit. Septoria does not infect fruit. Septoria leaf spots have light tan centres with tiny black dots.' } RETURN NONE;
INSERT RELATION INTO looks_like { id: looks_like:[disease:`tomato_septoria_leaf_spot`, disease:`tomato_early_blight`], in: disease:`tomato_septoria_leaf_spot`, out: disease:`tomato_early_blight`, how_to_tell: 'Septoria spots have light tan centres with tiny black dots, best seen with a hand lens. Septoria rarely causes yellowing until spots are many. Early blight spots have dark rings like a target, and they grow larger and angular over time.' } RETURN NONE;
INSERT RELATION INTO looks_like { id: looks_like:[disease:`tomato_spider_mites`, disease:`tomato_whiteflies`], in: disease:`tomato_spider_mites`, out: disease:`tomato_whiteflies`, how_to_tell: 'Both live on the underside of the leaf and leave tiny pale or yellow feeding spots. Spider mites spin fine silk webbing; whiteflies do not. Whitefly adults are tiny insects with powdery white wings. Whitefly young are flat, oval, greenish-yellow scales, about 0.4 to 0.7 mm long, that stay stuck flat to the leaf; spider mites are tiny oval mites, often with two dark spots. Whiteflies leave sticky honeydew, on which black sooty mould grows; spider mites leave the leaves bronzed or bleached.' } RETURN NONE;
INSERT RELATION INTO looks_like { id: looks_like:[disease:`tomato_whiteflies`, disease:`tomato_spider_mites`], in: disease:`tomato_whiteflies`, out: disease:`tomato_spider_mites`, how_to_tell: 'Both live on the underside of the leaf and leave tiny pale or yellow feeding spots. Spider mites spin fine silk webbing; whiteflies do not. Whitefly adults are tiny insects with powdery white wings. Whitefly young are flat, oval, greenish-yellow scales, about 0.4 to 0.7 mm long, that stay stuck flat to the leaf; spider mites are tiny oval mites, often with two dark spots. Whiteflies leave sticky honeydew, on which black sooty mould grows; spider mites leave the leaves bronzed or bleached.' } RETURN NONE;
